# Reuse a named theorem about reciprocal products on nonzero rationals.
have fn inverse(x Q*) Q* = 1 / x
thm inverse_product:
    ? forall a Q*, b Q*:
        inverse(a * b) = inverse(a) * inverse(b)
    inverse(a * b) = 1 / (a * b)
    inverse(a) = 1 / a
    inverse(b) = 1 / b
    inverse(a) * inverse(b) = (1 / a) * (1 / b)
    (1 / a) * (1 / b) = 1 / (a * b)
by thm inverse_product(2, -3) => inverse(2 * (-3)) = inverse(2) * inverse(-3)
